From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Friedman <friedmanj98@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 08:14:27 -0400
Subject: fix: bind remote-frame audio mixers to their source

Default-device sinks use the local source frame whenever the main frame is
remote, but the mixer key still groups those sinks by the remote main
frame. Removing the frame which owns the shared sink can therefore leave
sibling media attached to a closed audio output clock.

Include the source frame in a default-device mixer identity whenever its
main frame is remote. Classify the two default-device aliases before
explicit device IDs so the aliases remain equivalent without violating
strict weak ordering. Local-main-frame mixers and explicit devices retain
their existing sharing behavior.

The regression tests verify same-source alias sharing, separation and
independent teardown for sibling sources under a remote main frame, and
strict ordering around the communications device. The playback stall and
owner-dependent sink teardown have been reproduced on Windows and macOS,
matching the platform-independent sink ownership rule corrected here.

This patch is intended to be upstreamed to Chromium and removed after the
fix rolls into Electron.

diff --git a/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/media/audio/audio_renderer_mixer_manager.h b/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/media/audio/audio_renderer_mixer_manager.h
index 2894eaed100f13a885bc1d3ddeb904c1d9688d43..b010267694610c2f3ec4bb53a726da84c0614e7e 100644
--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/media/audio/audio_renderer_mixer_manager.h
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/media/audio/audio_renderer_mixer_manager.h
@@ -141,11 +141,30 @@ class BLINK_MODULES_EXPORT AudioRendererMixerManager final
         return a.params.effects() < b.params.effects();
       }
 
-      if (media::AudioDeviceDescription::IsDefaultDevice(a.device_id) &&
-          media::AudioDeviceDescription::IsDefaultDevice(b.device_id)) {
-        // Both device IDs represent the same default device => do not compare
-        // them. We can skip the `source_frame_token` check in this case since
-        // the default device is always authorized.
+      const bool a_device_is_default =
+          media::AudioDeviceDescription::IsDefaultDevice(a.device_id);
+      const bool b_device_is_default =
+          media::AudioDeviceDescription::IsDefaultDevice(b.device_id);
+
+      if (a_device_is_default != b_device_is_default) {
+        // Keep the aliases for the default device in one ordering class.
+        // Otherwise, "" and "default" could compare differently around an
+        // explicit device ID.
+        return a_device_is_default;
+      }
+
+      if (a_device_is_default && a.main_frame_token.Is<RemoteFrameToken>() &&
+          a.source_frame_token != b.source_frame_token) {
+        // A remote main frame cannot own the sink, so GetSink() binds it to
+        // the local source frame instead. Match the mixer's lifetime to that
+        // source frame.
+        return a.source_frame_token < b.source_frame_token;
+      }
+
+      if (a_device_is_default) {
+        // Both device IDs represent the same default device. Outside the
+        // source-bound remote-main-frame case above, preserve sharing and
+        // ignore the alias spelling.
         return false;
       }
 
